# contracts/api.http — run 2026-09-07-manual-mark-flown, T-001.
#
# Every request/response shape of PUT /api/flights/:id/planned-leg-status,
# frozen. design.md §5. Reference artifact; not executed by the build.
#
# The bodies below use the live logbook's real ids so T-004's curl matrix and
# T-005's re-run can be written straight off this file. Run them against a
# SCRATCH server on port 3100 with a COPY of the database — never against the
# user's server on 3000 (.claude/ENVIRONMENT.md).
#
# Every error body is {"error": "<text>"} — the shape every handler in
# src/server.ts already uses. The texts are frozen; message drift is a review
# finding.

### 1. FORWARD — the stuck case this feature exists for.
# flight 56: manual link, ended, leg 12 status 'planned'. §1.3 row 1.
PUT http://localhost:3100/api/flights/56/planned-leg-status
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "flown" }

# 200 — the updated PlannedLegWithChildren (getPlannedLegById(12)), abridged:
# {
#   "id": 12, "trip_id": 1, "seq": 8,
#   "status": "flown",
#   "destination_ident": "PAJN",
#   "destination_lat": 58.354721, "destination_lon": -134.578491,
#   "arrival_deviation_nm": 0.3,
#   "linked_flight_id": 56,
#   "waypoints": [ ... ], "alternates": [ ... ]
# }
#
# Side effects: exactly one UPDATE of planned_legs(status, arrival_deviation_nm).
# flights.planned_leg_id (12), planned_leg_link_source ('manual'), trip_id (1)
# and planned_leg_prev_trip_id (1) are UNCHANGED.


### 2. REVERSE — back to planned, deviation cleared, link kept. §1.3 row 2.
PUT http://localhost:3100/api/flights/56/planned-leg-status
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "planned" }

# 200 — same payload with:
#   "status": "planned", "arrival_deviation_nm": null, "linked_flight_id": 56
#
# GET /api/flights/56 still shows planned_leg_id 12 and
# planned_leg_link_source "manual". THE REVERSE MUST NOT UNLINK.


### 3. Idempotence / round trip.
# Repeating request 1 after request 2 restores arrival_deviation_nm 0.3 exactly
# (design.md §2.2, the round-trip identity). Repeating request 1 twice in a row
# gives 409 LEG_NOT_PLANNED on the second, because the leg is no longer
# 'planned'. That is the 409 the UI must render inline (design.md §8.4).


### 4. REFUSED — auto link. flight 48 -> leg 5. §1.3 row 10.
PUT http://localhost:3100/api/flights/48/planned-leg-status
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "planned" }

# 409
# { "error": "Flight 48 was not linked to its planned leg by hand: only a hand-linked flight's leg can be closed by hand" }


### 5. REFUSED — flight still in the air. §1.3 row 5.
# Construct in the scratch copy: a flight with end_time NULL, a manual link.
PUT http://localhost:3100/api/flights/<in-air-id>/planned-leg-status
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "flown" }

# 409
# { "error": "Flight <in-air-id> has not ended: its planned leg is closed at touchdown" }


### 6. REFUSED — leg already flown, request 'flown'. §1.3 row 2, forward cell.
PUT http://localhost:3100/api/flights/56/planned-leg-status
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "flown" }

# 409 (when leg 12 is already 'flown')
# { "error": "Planned leg 12 is 'flown', not 'planned': only a planned leg can be marked flown by hand" }


### 7. REFUSED — diverted or skipped leg, either direction. §1.3 rows 3, 4.
# { "status": "flown"   } -> 409 "Planned leg N is 'diverted', not 'planned': only a planned leg can be marked flown by hand"
# { "status": "planned" } -> 409 "Planned leg N is 'diverted', not 'flown': only a flown leg can be returned to planned"
# Same two texts with 'skipped' in place of 'diverted'.
# The route out of 'diverted'/'skipped' remains Unlink (design.md §1.7, §1.8).


### 8. REFUSED — flight has no planned leg. §1.5.
PUT http://localhost:3100/api/flights/<unlinked-id>/planned-leg-status
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "flown" }

# 409
# { "error": "Flight <unlinked-id> is not linked to a planned leg" }


### 9. 404 — unknown flight id.
PUT http://localhost:3100/api/flights/999999/planned-leg-status
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "flown" }

# 404
# { "error": "Flight not found" }


### 10. 400 — non-numeric id.
PUT http://localhost:3100/api/flights/abc/planned-leg-status
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "flown" }

# 400
# { "error": "Invalid id" }


### 11. 400 — bad or missing status. Checked BEFORE the flight 404 (§5.4 step 2).
PUT http://localhost:3100/api/flights/56/planned-leg-status
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "diverted" }

# 400
# { "error": "status must be 'flown' or 'planned'" }
#
# Same 400 for {}, {"status":"skipped"}, {"status":null}, {"status":1}.
# 'diverted' is NOT settable by hand at any path (design.md §1.7, §3.4).


### 12. 409 — the race (design.md §4.3), reachable only by concurrent unlink.
# { "error": "Planned leg 12 cannot be closed by hand: it has no linked flight" }
# { "error": "Planned leg 12 cannot be closed by hand: its flight was not linked by hand" }
# { "error": "Planned leg 12 cannot be closed by hand: its flight has not ended" }


### 13. UNCHANGED — the F-1 differential. Must be byte-identical to a server
### built from `git archive HEAD`. design.md §5.6, must-not-change M-4.
PATCH http://localhost:3100/api/planned-legs/<unlinked-leg>
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "skipped" }
# 200, the leg

# { "status": "planned" } -> 200, the leg
# { "status": "flown"   } -> 400 { "error": "status must be 'planned' or 'skipped'" }
#
PATCH http://localhost:3100/api/planned-legs/12
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "planned" }
# 409 { "error": "Planned leg 12 cannot have its status changed: linked to flight 56" }
# ^ still a 409 even though the NEW endpoint allows this leg. The new capability
#   exists only at the new path.
